.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_ensemble" "fuzzygene_ensemble"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_ensemble \- Ensemble (resampled boolean structure) prediction of virtual perturbations.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_ensemble(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
\fBgenes\fR as string, 
\fBmode\fR as string = "knockout", 
\fBsamples\fR as integer = 16, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Ensemble (resampled boolean structure) prediction of virtual perturbations.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained model built with \fBpbnRegularization != "none"\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgenes\fB \fR\- the genes to perturb. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- \fBknockout\fR (default), \fBknockdown\fR or \fBoverexpression\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsamples\fB \fR\- how many PBN resamples; <= 0 falls back to the configured value. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a named list of data.frames
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Each sample rebuilds the network by drawing one rule per target gene from the
 probabilistic boolean network according to its CoD derived probability, and then solves
 the continuous perturbation again. The spread of the resulting states therefore measures
 **structural uncertainty** (which regulatory logic the data supports), not numerical noise.
 


 


 Returns a named list:
 


 
- \fBtable\fR: one row per (perturbation, gene) with \fBmean\fR / \fBsd\fR /
 \fBlower\fR (5%) / \fBupper\fR (95%) / \fBsign_agreement\fR / \fBhigh_fraction\fR / \fBreference\fR;
- \fBsummary\fR: one row per perturbation with \fBsamples\fR /
 \fBconverged_fraction\fR / \fBdegenerate\fR / \fBnotes\fR;
- \fBattractors\fR: the boolean attractor period distribution
 (\fBperturbation\fR / \fBperiod\fR / \fBcount\fR), zero rows when no cycle was detected.


 


 \fBsign_agreement\fR is the single most useful column: about 0.5 means the direction of that
 gene's response is decided by the model noise, so it must not be reported as a finding.
.PP
